; ============================================================================
; GOLDEN_00_ROOT.ERB - golden run entry point
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Purpose : L2 spec-conformance golden fixture for eratw-android.
;
; LAUNCH  : AUTOMATIC. This file defines a `#PRI` `@EVENTFIRST` handler
;           (below) and the engine dispatches it itself on NEW GAME - no game
;           file is touched, no console command is needed (none exists, see
;           CONSOLE block). Chain: title -> openning input 0 = new game
;           (Process.cs endOpenning:2167-2180; the engine adds chara 0 at
;           :2172-2176) -> beginFirst() (Process.cs:2201) ->
;           callFunction("EVENTFIRST", force:true) (Process.cs:2207).
;           EVENTFIRST is an engine event name (IdentifierDictionary.cs
;           IsEventLabelName :72-89); event functions allow unlimited
;           same-name definitions and ALL of them execute, ordered by bucket
;           #ONLY(0) -> #PRI(1) -> normal(2) -> #LATER(3), load order inside
;           a bucket (LabelDictionary.cs:70-105 + 185-239 bucket split,
;           CalledFunction.cs:228-243 ShiftNext group 0..3; rule also in
;           specs/loader.md appendix D rule 2 / D.4). `#PRI` is legal on
;           event labels only and is parsed at LogicalLineParser.cs:81-107.
;           Why bucket #PRI and NOT #LATER: the game's own normal-bucket
;           @EVENTFIRST (ERB/SYSTEM.ERB:8) ends with `BEGIN SHOP`, and
;           ProcessState.Begin() clears the whole call stack
;           (ProcessState.cs:219-271, functionList.Clear() :258-266) - any
;           bucket after the normal one would never run. With #PRI our
;           handler executes BEFORE the game's init: the suite's DELALLCHARA
;           then wipes only the engine-created starter charas, and the game's
;           own NEWGAME (normal bucket, after us) rebuilds its roster, so the
;           engine-side anomalies the suite provokes (if any) print AFTER
;           `=== END ===` and are outside the golden range (runbook sec 5).
;           Why NOT @EVENTLOAD (A11b warning upheld, not overridden):
;           EVENTLOAD is dispatched on EVERY save load (Process.cs:2674), and
;           the suite runs DELALLCHARA + SAVEDATA; `#LATER` cannot be proven
;           last because bucket 3 already holds 5 game #LATER handlers
;           ordered by load sequence among themselves (specs/loader.md D.4
;           note: EVENTLOAD 32->84->1367->260->2->32->63->91->387), and a
;           re-run while a real save is loaded destroys that game (the #DIM
;           guard is per-process only). @EVENTTRAIN/@EVENTCOM/@EVENTCOMEND/
;           @EVENTTURNEND all have game handlers touching chara state and
;           none is guaranteed on a fresh start; EVENTFIRST is the only
;           forced (force:true) fire-and-once event of the new-game path.
; CONSOLE : THE SUITE CANNOT BE STARTED FROM THE EMUERA CONSOLE (A11b proof,
;           kept for the record). `@X` -> EmueraConsole.doSystemCommand
;           (strips the leading `@` at :1644) -> DebugCommand(:2167+); text
;           that fails ParseLine is evaluated as an EXPRESSION (:2185-2190,
;           hence `@GOLDEN_ROOT` -> cannot-resolve-identifier), and a parsed
;           InstructionLine must pass all gates at :2204-2216; CALL/JUMP/
;           GOTO/CALLEVENT/RESTART families all carry FLOW_CONTROL (flag
;           definitions FunctionIdentifier.cs:3721/3725, ctor OR
;           :4200-4206) and are rejected; the only console-reachable call
;           statements CALLF/CALLFORMF/TRYCALLF/TRYCALLFORMF (flag 38,
;           :1114/:1245) accept `#FUNCTION` methods only
;           (IdentifierDictionary.cs:555-559) and a method body may contain
;           only METHOD_SAFE statements (ErbLoader.cs:1032-1036), which would
;           delete exactly the statements this suite exists to cover.
;           Collection instead: the suite itself runs
;           `OUTPUTLOG "GOLDEN_ROOT_LOG.txt"` right after `=== END ===`
;           (EmueraConsole.cs:1654-1656 routes OUTPUTLOG straight to
;           OutputSystemLog, :3484 full GetLog replay). Snapshotting from
;           inside the suite is required: once control returns, the game's
;           normal @EVENTFIRST reaches BEGIN SHOP and the console log is
;           cleared, so a console-side `@OUTPUTLOG` afterwards only contains
;           the game's own screens (observed run4). GOLDEN_09's
;           `OUTPUTLOG "GOLDEN_LOG.txt"` remains a mid-run snapshot
;           (sections 1-9 only) and is redundant.
; Boot    : `@GOLDEN_BOOT` (below) is a guarded ONE-SHOT wrapper of
;           `CALL GOLDEN_ROOT`: `#DIM GOLDEN_BOOT_DONE` right after the label
;           line = private var of that function (proven load-safe pattern,
;           same shape as GOLDEN_01 #DIM GIDX) and keeps its value across
;           calls, so any repeated EVENTFIRST dispatch (e.g. a later
;           `BEGIN FIRST`) re-enters the hook but returns without re-running
;           the suite. For the semi-manual section, temporarily edit the
;           hook body below to `CALL GOLDEN_BOOT_MANUAL` (fixture edit, NOT
;           a game edit) - `@GOLDEN_BOOT_MANUAL` is the same one-shot wrapper
;           around GOLDEN_07. Never leave these GOLDEN_*.ERB files in the
;           game's ERB/ outside a capture session: every NEW GAME while they
;           are present runs the suite (and deletes charas); see runbook sec 2.
; Rules   : - deterministic only: no RAND outside the seeded RANDOMIZE
;             section in GOLDEN_05_DATA.ERB.
;           - every section prints "=== SECTION:xxx ===" headers.
;           - output is ASCII except values that come from the game's
;             own CSV data (see GOLDEN_04_CHARA.ERB).
; Coverage map and run instructions: docs/golden-runbook.md (sec 2/3 = launch)
; ============================================================================
; Auto-launch hook: engine event function, #PRI bucket of @EVENTFIRST.
; Runs BEFORE the game's normal-bucket @EVENTFIRST (ERB/SYSTEM.ERB:8, which
; ends with BEGIN SHOP and would clear the call stack via ProcessState.Begin,
; ProcessState.cs:258-266, killing any later bucket). Idempotency is ensured
; by the GOLDEN_BOOT guard below. Do NOT convert this to #LATER/normal.
@EVENTFIRST
#PRI
	CALL GOLDEN_BOOT
@GOLDEN_BOOT
	#DIM GOLDEN_BOOT_DONE
	; One-shot bootstrap for the in-game call site (see LAUNCH above).
	; `#DIM <var>` right after a label line = private var of that function,
	; proven load-safe pattern (same shape as GOLDEN_01 #DIM GIDX); it keeps
	; its value across calls, so re-entering GOLDEN_BOOT is a no-op.
	IF GOLDEN_BOOT_DONE == 1
		RETURN
	ENDIF
	GOLDEN_BOOT_DONE = 1
	CALL GOLDEN_ROOT
@GOLDEN_BOOT_MANUAL
	#DIM GOLDEN_BOOT_MANUAL_DONE
	; One-shot bootstrap for GOLDEN_07_INPUT_MANUAL (semi-manual collection).
	IF GOLDEN_BOOT_MANUAL_DONE == 1
		RETURN
	ENDIF
	GOLDEN_BOOT_MANUAL_DONE = 1
	CALL GOLDEN_INPUT_MANUAL
@GOLDEN_ROOT
	PRINTL === GOLDEN RUN START ===
	PRINTL === SECTION:ROOT-INFO ===
	PRINTFORML EMUERA_VERSION=%EMUERA_VERSION%
	PRINTFORML MONEYLABEL=%MONEYLABEL%
	PRINTFORML GAMEBASE_TITLE=%GAMEBASE_TITLE%
	PRINTFORML GAMEBASE_VERSION={GAMEBASE_VERSION}
	PRINTFORML GAMEBASE_GAMECODE={GAMEBASE_GAMECODE}
	PRINTFORML SAVENOS_FUNC={SAVENOS()}
	PRINTFORML __INT_MAX__={__INT_MAX__}
	PRINTFORML __INT_MIN__={__INT_MIN__}
	CALL GOLDEN_BASIC
	CALL GOLDEN_PRINT
	CALL GOLDEN_FLOW
	CALL GOLDEN_CHARA
	CALL GOLDEN_DATA
	CALL GOLDEN_RNG
	CALL GOLDEN_INPUT_AUTO
	CALL GOLDEN_IO
	CALL GOLDEN_MISC
	CALL GOLDEN_XMLMAP
	CALL GOLDEN_GVIEW
	CALL GOLDEN_SYMBOLS
	PRINTL === END ===
	; Snapshot the whole console replay before control returns to the game:
	; the game's own @EVENTFIRST (BEGIN SHOP) clears the console log, so a
	; console-side @OUTPUTLOG afterwards only sees the game's screens.
	OUTPUTLOG "GOLDEN_ROOT_LOG.txt"
	; Fault-isolated probe: if this aborts, === END === is already in the log.
	CALL GOLDEN_XML_PROBE
	; NOTE: GOLDEN_INPUT_MANUAL (WAIT/ONEINPUT/TWAIT/INPUTANY/PRINTDATAW...)
	; must be executed separately from its own call site (CALL
	; GOLDEN_INPUT_MANUAL, or one-shot CALL GOLDEN_BOOT_MANUAL) - the console
	; cannot launch any plain label; see LAUNCH block in the header.
	; NOTE: GOLDEN_SYMBOLS also registers 3 x @EVENTTURNEND (bucket-order test);
	; its markers appear when a turn ends, not during this run - see runbook section 8.
